      "desc": "Assign permissions to **groups** (humans) and **roles** (workloads); avoid user-attached policies. Enforce **least privilege**, prefer federation and temporary credentials, and use tags or **permissions boundaries** to constrain scope. Review regularly to remove direct user policies and right-size access.",
      "references": [
        "https://hub.prowler.com/check/iam_policy_attached_only_to_group_or_roles"
      ]
    },
    "risk_details": "Directly attached user policies hinder centralized control and cause privilege creep. If a user is compromised, excessive rights enable data exposure, resource tampering, and lateral movement, harming **confidentiality** and **integrity**. Revocation is error-prone, weakening **separation of duties** and auditability.",
    "time": 1793826847,
